{{#extend "layout-video"}}
  {{#content "intro"}}
    <h1>
      A well behaved dog
    </h1>
    <h2>
      is a joy to live with
    </h2>
    <h3>
      Gaynor Probert at A1K9 Behaviour and Training Academy.
      <br />
      Improving relationships between dogs and their owners through
      <strong>
        behaviour modification
      </strong>
      and
      <strong>
        training
      </strong>
      .
    </h3>
  {{/content}}
  {{#content "main"}}
    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="grid items-center gap-8 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-7">
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl sm:text-3xl">
            Behavioural Consultations
          </h2>
          <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-ink-600">
            Behavioural problems are a sign that the relationship with your dog
            is off balance. Gaynor Probert
            <strong class="text-ink-900">
              CFBA practitioner of the year 2014
            </strong>
            has the skills and the experience to give you the specialist help
            that is required to find the quickest way to that happy relationship
            that you have always wanted.
          </p>
          <a href="/behavioural-consultations" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            Find out more
            <svg
              class="size-4"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <path d="m7 4 6 6-6 6" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-5">
          <img
            src="/images/index/gaynor-probert-award-v1.webp"
            alt="Gaynor Probert with her CFBA Practitioner of the Year 2014 award"
            width="500"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="h-auto w-full rounded-card"
          />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="grid items-center gap-8 border-t border-sand-200 pt-16 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-5">
          <img
            src="/images/index/peek-a-boo-dog-1.webp"
            alt="A dog and owner during an A1K9 obedience training class"
            width="500"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="h-auto w-full rounded-card"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-7">
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl sm:text-3xl">
            Dog Obedience Training
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-ink-600">
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/puppy-socialisation" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  Puppy Socialisation classes
                </a>
              </strong>
              - For pups up to the age of 6 months, Gaynor Probert will teach you
              the most important aspects of your dog's education and how to help
              him develop into the well behaved and balanced pet you have always
              wanted. It is good fun and all the family can join in.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/junior-obedience" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  Junior Course
                </a>
              </strong>
              - For puppies between the age of 6 and 12 months the junior course
              is suitable for all breeds of dogs it is a natural progression from
              puppy classes.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/bronze-obedience" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  Bronze Obedience Course
                </a>
              </strong>
              - For dogs 12 months of age and upward, teach your dog to walk on a
              slack lead without pulling and to come back when called are the two
              priorities in this course. We also teach you how to prevent your dog
              barging through the door first when you are going out.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/silver-obedience" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  Silver Obedience Course
                </a>
              </strong>
              - In this course you learn how to train your dog to go at your pace
              and to come back to you when there are distractions around. You will
              also be taught how to get your dog to stay when told. It is in this
              course that we start the agility training, an activity that the dogs
              love.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/gold-obedience" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  Gold Obedience Course
                </a>
              </strong>
              - In this course you will learn how to get your dog to walk by your
              side off lead and come back to your side when you are walking. We
              add another interest, how to get your dog to find his toy when it is
              amongst others, The agility training continues, which your dog will
              love.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/platinum-obedience" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  Platinum Obedience Course
                </a>
              </strong>
              - Some of the techniques taught on this course are - changing pace
              while weaving through people and their dogs, staying while you go
              out of sight and distance control and emergency down. The agility
              training is now done off lead as you now have full control of your
              dog.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong class="text-ink-900">
                <a href="/courses/one-to-one" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                  One to One
                </a>
              </strong>
              - A one to one with Gaynor Probert offers you a unique opportunity
              to expand your understanding of your dog and to address any
              obedience that you may be having problems with.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-sand-200 pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-2xl sm:text-3xl">
          Gaynor is
        </h2>
        <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-base">
              A practitioner with the
              <a href="http://www.cfba.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                Canine and Feline Behaviour Association
              </a>
            </h3>
            <div class="card flex flex-1 flex-col gap-4 p-5">
              <a href="http://www.cfba.co.uk/gaynorprobert.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <img
                  src="/images/about/CFBA-v1.webp"
                  alt="Gaynor is CFBA accredited"
                  width="260"
                  height="173"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  class="h-auto w-full rounded-card"
                />
              </a>
              <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between gap-4">
                <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600">
                  <p>
                    These Middlesex University accredited dog behaviour and
                    training accreditations represent the highest levels of
                    specific canine behaviour qualifications available in Britain
                    today.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    They are one of the few associations that are recognised by
                    dog insurance companies for canine behavioural problems.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <a
                  href="http://www.cfba.co.uk/gaynorprobert.html"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  class="btn btn-primary btn-sm self-start"
                >
                  Website
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-base">
              A full Member of the
              <a href="http://bipdt.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                British Institute of Professional Dog Trainers
              </a>
            </h3>
            <div class="card flex flex-1 flex-col gap-4 p-5">
              <a href="http://bipdt.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <img
                  src="/images/about/BIPDT-V1.webp"
                  alt="Gaynor is BIPDT accredited"
                  width="260"
                  height="251"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  class="h-auto w-full rounded-card"
                />
              </a>
              <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between gap-4">
                <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600">
                  <p>
                    Founded in 1974 to improve the standards of care and
                    understanding, conditions and training of working and pet
                    dogs, it is the longest established governing body in this
                    field of work. These certificates are not awarded lightly. MBIPDT
                    is the highest award of the institute and qualifies members to
                    teach at the highest level.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <a
                  href="http://bipdt.org.uk/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  class="btn btn-primary btn-sm self-start"
                >
                  Website
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-base">
              A Master Trainer with the
              <a href="http://www.godt.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                Guild of Dog Trainers
              </a>
            </h3>
            <div class="card flex flex-1 flex-col gap-4 p-5">
              <a href="http://www.godt.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <img
                  src="/images/about/guild-of-dog-trainers-v1.webp"
                  alt="Gaynor is accredited by the guild of dog trainers"
                  width="260"
                  height="286"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  class="h-auto w-full rounded-card"
                />
              </a>
              <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between gap-4">
                <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600">
                  <p>
                    The Guild of dog trainers is an independent professional body
                    whose values include being committed to maintaining and
                    improving the quality of dog training, behaviour and companion
                    dog ownership in Britain. Master trainer is the highest level
                    of certification and qualifies recipients to teach at the
                    highest level.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <a
                  href="http://www.godt.org.uk/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  class="btn btn-primary btn-sm self-start"
                >
                  Website
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-base">
              A member of the
              <a href="http://www.ntipdu.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-700 underline">
                National Training Inspectorate for Professional Dog Users
              </a>
            </h3>
            <div class="card flex flex-1 flex-col gap-4 p-5">
              <a href="http://www.ntipdu.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <img
                  src="/images/about/NTIPDU-v1.webp"
                  alt="Gaynor is NTIPDU accredited"
                  width="223"
                  height="225"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  class="h-auto w-full rounded-card"
                />
              </a>
              <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between gap-4">
                <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600">
                  <p>
                    The NTIPDU was formed to promote professionalism, set and
                    maintain standards and to assist all governing bodies within
                    the security industry, it has progressed through the years and
                    with the input of government departments is now a leader in
                    the development of canine related courses.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <a
                  href="http://www.ntipdu.org/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  class="btn btn-primary btn-sm self-start"
                >
                  Website
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-sand-200 pt-16">
        <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="card flex flex-col items-center gap-4 p-6 text-center">
            <a href="https://www.facebook.com/A1K9PDT?fref=ts" target="fb" rel="noopener">
              <img
                src="/images/index/facebook-v1.webp"
                alt="Find us on Facebook"
                width="140"
                height="140"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                class="size-20 rounded-full"
              />
            </a>
            <h2 class="text-xl">
              <a href="https://www.facebook.com/A1K9PDT?fref=ts" target="fb" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-700 no-underline hover:underline">
                Facebook
              </a>
            </h2>
            <p class="text-ink-600">
              Follow me on facebook for our most recent photos, stories,
              interesting links, etc.
            </p>
            <a
              href="https://www.facebook.com/A1K9PDT?fref=ts"
              target="fb"
              rel="noopener"
              class="btn btn-secondary"
            >
              Open Page »
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="card flex flex-col items-center gap-4 p-6 text-center">
            <a href="/contact/">
              <img
                src="/images/index/find-us-v1.webp"
                alt="How to find A1K9"
                width="140"
                height="140"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                class="size-20 rounded-full"
              />
            </a>
            <h2 class="text-xl">
              <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-700 no-underline hover:underline">
                Find Us
              </a>
            </h2>
            <p class="text-ink-600">
              Directions on how to find us.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact/">
              Find Us »
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="card flex flex-col items-center gap-4 p-6 text-center">
            <a href="tel:+447798500390">
              <img
                src="/images/index/tel-v1.webp"
                alt="Call Me"
                width="140"
                height="140"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                class="size-20 rounded-full"
              />
            </a>
            <h2 class="text-xl">
              <a href="tel:+447798500390" class="text-brand-700 no-underline hover:underline">
                Call Me
              </a>
            </h2>
            <p class="text-ink-600">
              If you would like more information about anything that you have
              read, I would love to hear from you!
            </p>
            <a
              class="btn btn-secondary"
              href="tel:+447798500390"
            >
              Telephone »
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  {{/content}}
{{/extend}}
